1
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:08,390
♪Don't stay trapped inside your room♪

2
00:00:08,390 --> 00:00:09,790
♪Outside the window,
the rain has cleared♪

3
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:11,070
♪Set reality aside♪

4
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:12,390
♪Follow your heart♪

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:13,750
♪What you've been longing
for is right ahead♪

6
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:15,230
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

7
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:18,110
♪Just be a little braver♪

8
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:20,870
♪Come closer, come closer♪

9
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:23,950
♪There's a little spark
shining in your eyes♪

10
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:26,070
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

11
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:29,790
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

12
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:33,820
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=
(Bonus Edition)

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:39,000
I want to grill those chicken wings now.

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,120
Otherwise,

15
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:40,840
they might go bad.

16
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:43,080
Regular parchment paper should work.

17
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:43,600
Right?

18
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:44,320
Yeah.

19
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,120
Hello.

20
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:47,260
I'm grilling chicken wings.

21
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:47,920
You can try some later.

22
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,200
You're so thoughtful.

23
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:55,120
What do you have to eat? What's this?

24
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:56,400
I'm grilling chicken wings.

25
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:57,720
Nice.

26
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:00,240
Hello.

27
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,040
(Looks back)

28
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:02,520
Hi.

29
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:03,240
Xing,

30
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:04,680
I just went to your room to find you.

31
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:05,640
You weren't there.

32
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,520
Do you want
some grilled chicken wings later?

33
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:08,400
Sure.

34
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:10,100
(Glances)

35
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:11,920
What's up?

36
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:16,240
Is tomorrow going to be sunny?

37
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:17,560
Why?

38
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:19,920
Do you have plans tomorrow?

39
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:20,560
Who?

40
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:21,320
You.

41
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:22,640
No.

42
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,000
Do you want to go stargazing?

43
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:28,020
(Tugs)

44
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:29,520
What's up?

45
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:32,100
(Smiles)

46
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,160
Sunday works.

47
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,200
We can go stargazing Sunday night.

48
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:35,820
(Nods)

49
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:39,320
What about tonight?

50
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,120
Not today.

51
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:43,400
Today's coin gets you the room tomorrow.

52
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,720
You want to use yours?

53
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,040
It's fine. I'll use mine first.

54
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,120
You can keep it for now.

55
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:50,900
(Carrying Master Kong Jasmine Coin
all the time)

56
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:54,020
(Stares)

57
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:01,240
What do you have in your hand?

58
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:01,960
Let me see.

59
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:03,120
Is that the Master Kong Jasmine Coin?

60
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,280
No.

61
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,040
What is it?

62
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,200
I'm not telling you.

63
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,280
I'll wash it for you. Come on.

64
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:12,920
Okay.

65
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:13,640
(Helps)

66
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:16,080
Zhao Xilun's gotten more thoughtful lately.

67
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:18,000
Have I not always been thoughtful?

68
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,200
I never noticed.

69
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:20,600
Zhao Xilun isn't thoughtful?

70
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:21,360
(Just kidding)
You're kidding.

71
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,160
Zhao Xilun isn't thoughtful?

72
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:25,360
(Just kidding +2)
He's one of the most thoughtful guys.

73
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,840
How many pieces should I cut it into?

74
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:32,840
Well...

75
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:34,180
(Looks around)

76
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:35,220
(Shy)

77
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:38,040
Oh, I'm not listening.

78
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:39,420
(Leaves)

79
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:41,440
Do you want anything else to eat?

80
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:42,480
I'm good.

81
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:44,360
I'll just have some of theirs.

82
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:44,880
Okay.

83
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:45,920
We can have some of theirs.

84
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:47,840
We're planning to mooch off your food.

85
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:49,200
Do you want some toast?

86
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:50,160
Sure.

87
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,240
We can make some.

88
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:52,960
Do you want some toast?

89
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:53,680
(Asks)

90
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:54,760
Do you want some?

91
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:56,080
If you want, I'll have some with you.

92
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:57,200
If you don't, then forget it.

93
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:58,240
(Looks)
We'll see tomorrow.

94
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:01,640
See? I asked if he wanted some.

95
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:02,720
He won't even say whether he does.

96
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:03,480
What?

97
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,280
Do you guys want some toast?

98
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,000
Toast?

99
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:11,280
That one.

100
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:13,280
Sure.

101
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:17,720
(Teases)
Cui Yihang doesn't really want any.

102
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:19,320
I do. It's fine.

103
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,000
(Hands it over)
You eat first.

104
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:22,780
I'll wait for Si.

105
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:23,580
I'll make some in a bit.

106
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,840
Hello.

107
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,360
What are you doing?

108
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,680
Stuffing our faces!

109
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:36,160
I can't hold out.
I'm gonna cook some noodles.

110
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,280
I really can't hold out.

111
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:40,560
Guys, anyone want instant noodles?

112
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:42,520
Anyone want some instant noodles?

113
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:43,880
Who wants some?

114
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:45,600
(Joins immediately)
Sign up if you want some.

115
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,320
Come on. Who wants some?

116
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:48,320
(Looks over)

117
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:49,280
Two.

118
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:49,640
Two of us.

119
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:50,560
Two.

120
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,400
Do you guys want some instant noodles?

121
00:03:53,660 --> 00:03:54,340
(Nods)

122
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,280
Instant noodles?

123
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:57,600
I'd love some.

124
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:58,440
Sure.

125
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:59,200
Instant noodles?

126
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:00,000
Absolutely.

127
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,880
Then let's do it.

128
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:03,480
Thanks, Yu Yang.

129
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:05,040
Yu Yang is so thoughtful.

130
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:09,120
I've noticed that when Yu Yang cooks,

131
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:09,960
he's especially cheerful.

132
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:10,560
He's always so happy.

133
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:11,920
The happiest part of his day

134
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:12,720
is when he's cooking.

135
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:14,960
He's so good at it.

136
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:17,560
The prince is here.

137
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:18,560
Really.

138
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:19,440
The prince.

139
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:20,600
We have the prince.

140
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,320
Well, we have the prince.

141
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:25,080
We have the prince here.

142
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:29,000
And you look like the Black Fairy.

143
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,680
Black Fairy Yue.

144
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:34,560
Actually,
I can do the Black Fairy laugh.

145
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:36,440
Come on, show us.

146
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:38,100
(Glances)

147
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,560
That's a little scary.

148
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:45,320
Do I sound like her?

149
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:47,240
That was hilarious.

150
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:50,220
(Looks over)

151
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,880
Isn't Meng downstairs?

152
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:53,280
She's upstairs. I just saw her.

153
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:54,400
What's she doing?

154
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:55,400
She's in her room.

155
00:04:58,480 --> 00:04:59,920
It smells so good, Yu Yang.

156
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:01,200
You're amazing.

157
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:02,880
Thanks. That's enough.

158
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:05,640
Is this for me?

159
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:06,120
Yeah.

160
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:06,920
Thanks.

161
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,880
Sha Yue'er,
are you having the braised flavor?

162
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:11,560
Yeah.

163
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:12,640
I got one for you.

164
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:13,660
Thanks.

165
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:14,660
(Chicken wings are done)
Is it hot?

166
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:16,320
It's okay. A little hot.

167
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:17,880
It should be fine.

168
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:18,680
Okay, good.

169
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,280
I will...

170
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:20,440
We can just carry this over.

171
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:21,520
Sure.

172
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:24,560
I think it could use
a little more browning.

173
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:26,000
But it already looks delicious to me.

174
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:26,960
Let me take a bite.

175
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:27,440
Okay.

176
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,400
Super crispy.

177
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,360
What do you think?

178
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,440
It tastes great.

179
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:34,080
Really?

180
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,120
Are you sitting here?

181
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:37,960
Anywhere's fine.

182
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:38,280
Please.

183
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:39,360
Okay, you eat first.

184
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,080
Sit with me for a bit.

185
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:44,800
So good.

186
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:49,060
(Smiles)

187
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,320
I'll do it.

188
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,840
Don't burn yourself.
Which one do you want?

189
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:52,720
This one.

190
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:56,920
That was fast.

191
00:05:58,240 --> 00:05:59,200
This one's yours.

192
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:03,680
Sun Bohan, yours.

193
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:04,600
Okay, thanks.

194
00:06:07,060 --> 00:06:08,080
Why are you taking
so many pairs of chopsticks?

195
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:10,160
These are for Wu Siying and Cui Yihang.

196
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,240
Right, there.

197
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:11,880
Okay.

198
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:18,500
(Sitting together)

199
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:22,760
Smells so good.

200
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:24,000
This feels so nice.

201
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:24,760
It really does.

202
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:29,600
Smells so good.

203
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:31,760
So you're born in the Year of the Goat?

204
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:34,480
He's a 2004 baby.

205
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:35,800
But he was born in January.

206
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:36,880
So was I.

207
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,480
You're a Monkey.

208
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:39,160
Yeah.

209
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,000
You're a Monkey.

210
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:42,400
I was born on the first day
of the Chinese New Year.

211
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:44,160
- I'm a Monkey.
- I was born on the fifth day.

212
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:47,080
Then you're definitely a Monkey.

213
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:47,960
Being a Monkey is great.

214
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:50,440
Why is being a Monkey good?

215
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:51,960
I'm a Monkey too.

216
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:52,840
Being a Goat is good too.

217
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:55,680
You're not a Goat, are you?

218
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,480
I am.

219
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:58,000
Being a Goat is really good.

220
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:00,520
Men born in the Year of the Goat
have nothing but good qualities.

221
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,240
Wonderful.

222
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:08,780
(Follows)

223
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,320
You look...

224
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:11,920
You look pretty intimidating.

225
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:12,960
You look so serious.

226
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:13,520
Who?

227
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:14,000
You.

228
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:14,680
What?

229
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:16,040
When you're trying to look cool.

230
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,680
No. Aren't you looking in the mirror?

231
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:21,000
It didn't catch me.

232
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:21,800
I'm looking now.

233
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:22,600
Sometimes,

234
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,960
I think that look in your eyes means

235
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:25,720
you're upset.

236
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,160
No.

237
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,640
(Glances)

238
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:30,040
How could I be upset when I see you?

239
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:31,740
(How could I be upset when I see you?)

240
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:34,140
(Laughs)

241
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:35,440
If I smile like this,

242
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:38,920
it means I'm really happy.

243
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:39,680
But this kind of smile?

244
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:41,840
It's so fake.

245
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:42,800
Like this.

246
00:07:43,340 --> 00:07:44,380
(Imitating)

247
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:51,840
That was spot-on.

248
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:56,820
(Glances)

249
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:58,120
That mosquito bite on your eye

250
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,800
looks less swollen.

251
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,360
It's gone down a little.

252
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:02,840
Yeah.

253
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:06,060
(Glances)

254
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:09,160
Xing got bitten right
above her left eyelid.

255
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,800
Yeah. She even went out of her way
to cover it up today.

256
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:16,720
Okay.

257
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:22,320
Actually,

258
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:23,440
all the stuff you grilled every night,

259
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:26,600
there was always

260
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:29,000
quite a bit left over.

261
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,880
But none of it went to waste.

262
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:32,280
We took it all with us.

263
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:33,760
We took it back to our rooms to eat.

264
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:36,600
I can grill a little more next time

265
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:37,520
so everyone can eat together.

266
00:08:39,660 --> 00:08:41,980
(Smiles)

267
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:46,240
Did I tell you

268
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,000
about the time

269
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,240
I went
to use my Master Kong Jasmine Coin?

270
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:49,640
After I finished putting in the coin,

271
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:51,480
I had to go find the person
I wanted to invite.

272
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:53,400
And just as I got to the door,

273
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,680
Cui Yihang happened to open the door.

274
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:55,960
I asked him

275
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:58,360
which room Sun Bohan was in.

276
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:59,960
He said it was the one at the very end.

277
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:00,480
I said okay.

278
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,960
After standing there for three seconds,

279
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:02,580
he probably thought

280
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:03,980
I was a little too embarrassed
to knock on the door.

281
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:05,640
So he offered
to knock on the door for me.

282
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:09,400
I guess I shouldn't have someone else
knock for me,

283
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:11,400
but I really appreciated it.

284
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:13,400
What a coincidence.

285
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:14,880
Such a coincidence.

286
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:26,620
(Sun Qimeng returns to the room)

287
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:00,820
(Wu Xingying returns to the room)

288
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:01,800
Hi, Xing.

289
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:02,320
Welcome back.

290
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:03,120
Are you alone in the room?

291
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:03,560
Yeah.

292
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:10,520
Today's segment was pretty fun.

293
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,520
Yeah.

294
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:12,600
It was.

295
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:14,000
Did you have fun today?

296
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:14,720
Yeah.

297
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:16,760
While we were grilling the chicken wings,

298
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:17,880
I'd already counted everyone.

299
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:18,680
Then I suddenly realized

300
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:20,080
you were missing.

301
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:23,040
It just felt like everyone
was paired up.

302
00:10:23,380 --> 00:10:25,140
(Pause)

303
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:27,360
And then I started feeling

304
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:28,800
like wherever I went,

305
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:30,960
I was kind of getting in your way.

306
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:38,160
You don't need to think
so much about it.

307
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,200
No matter where you are,

308
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:41,000
we'll always notice you.

309
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:46,640
I mean,

310
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:48,400
Xing, you're so sensitive.

311
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:50,640
You were just standing there, crying.

312
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:53,160
I think being emotional is a good thing.

313
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:55,760
It means you can really put yourself
in other people's shoes.

314
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:59,360
It's because I saw how brave you were.

315
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:04,160
You're brave too.

316
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:07,000
I think everyone here is really brave.

317
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:11,840
For me, I've really gotten

318
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:13,280
to know everyone here.

319
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,720
It's like I've connected
with every single person.

320
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:17,680
And that makes me really happy.

321
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:19,200
So you actually

322
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:21,280
mean a lot to everyone.

323
00:11:23,450 --> 00:11:24,240
Oh my gosh.

324
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:25,840
I feel like I've made

325
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,160
so many great friends here.

326
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:28,840
I feel like I'm close with everyone.

327
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,080
I'm so happy.

328
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:43,320
Our relationship
is pretty special now.

329
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:44,360
With Sun Bohan?

330
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,080
Yeah.

331
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:47,480
Why is your relationship
with Sun Bohan special?

332
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:48,800
We're brothers-in-law.

333
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:49,400
What?

334
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:52,640
Brothers-in-law.

335
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:54,800
You're basically family now.

336
00:11:58,560 --> 00:11:59,760
That's actually pretty funny.

337
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,840
It feels weirdly familiar
when you see him now.

338
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:05,080
Yeah, your gatherings
are really something.

339
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:07,280
Future family gatherings
are gonna be pretty fun.

340
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:10,160
Si is so cute.

341
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:12,720
What are you doing?

342
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,360
(Laughing)
What? Why did you suddenly...

343
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:20,480
What's wrong?

344
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:23,000
It's all good.
They're all great, really.

345
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:23,960
Cui Kaiyi is great too.

346
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:24,920
Liang Renfang is even better.

347
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:26,920
They're all amazing.

348
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:33,860
(Mutual Date Sun Qimeng & Zhao Xilun)

349
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:35,200
Let's untie it.

350
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,680
It looks like it wants to play.

351
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:37,120
Okay.

352
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:38,720
By the way, have you ever had a pet?

353
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:39,360
No, I haven't.

354
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,560
But I always walk

355
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:42,040
my neighbor's dog with her.

356
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:42,640
Whenever

357
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:43,600
we want to chat,

358
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,240
we'll make plans
to walk the dog together.

359
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:47,960
Then you've got quite a bit
of experience with dogs.

360
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:49,760
I guess so.

361
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:51,220
Whenever I want to chat with her,

362
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:52,080
we just go walk the dog.

363
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:53,680
They're really social.

364
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,560
Yeah, they're getting
to know each other.

365
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:56,360
They're wagging their tails now.

366
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:58,960
Yeah, they're checking each other's age

367
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:01,000
and getting the basic info
about each other.

368
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:04,600
It's like checking
someone's social media.

369
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:05,680
(Laughing)
Seriously.

370
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:06,200
Yeah.

371
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:08,360
That's amazing.

372
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:09,720
Yeah.

373
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:12,120
You can split it in half.

374
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:12,840
Give each of them a piece.

375
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:15,280
Come on, you want some too.

376
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:16,480
See? You only care about food.

377
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:17,720
I knew it.

378
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:18,920
It does only care about food.

379
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:21,260
What about your friend's dog?

380
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:22,880
- Does it listen to her?
- It doesn't listen at all.

381
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:23,600
When we walk the dog,

382
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:24,680
it's basically the dog walking us.

383
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:25,720
We basically

384
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:27,440
end up running the whole time.

385
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:29,240
How old is it?

386
00:13:29,760 --> 00:13:30,760
It's a little over a year old.

387
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:32,100
And it's really naughty.

388
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:33,120
- A little over a year old?
- It'll just...

389
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:35,600
Yeah, it'll go after other dogs.

390
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,000
It'll keep barking at other dogs.

391
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,080
What kind of bark is it?

392
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:39,360
You know, is it "woof woof" or "awoo"?

393
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,040
Is it "woof woof" or "awoo"?

394
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:45,240
It's all kinds of sounds.

395
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:47,200
And it'd scare off the other dogs.

396
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:48,920
But sometimes, dogs get excited

397
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:49,480
when

398
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,520
they chase something

399
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:51,200
and start barking.

400
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:53,160
One is wagging its tail really fast,

401
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:54,560
and another is holding its tail up

402
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:55,400
and wagging it really fast.

403
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,680
Really fast wagging means it's on alert.

404
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:58,880
It might be ready to fight.

405
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:00,920
Yeah, but when they're just excited,

406
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:02,120
they usually wag it from side to side.

407
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,600
These two are both gentle dogs.

408
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:04,600
Yeah.

409
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:06,480
Why don't we play with them for a while?

410
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:06,880
Sure.

411
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:13,860
(Mutual Date Wu Siying & Cui Yihang)

412
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:18,120
Did you usually fly kites by yourself
when you were little?

413
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:21,280
No. I mostly flew kites at school.

414
00:14:21,280 --> 00:14:23,000
With your classmates?

415
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,040
Yeah, we had a Kite Festival.

416
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:27,200
Every year, we'd fly a small kite

417
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:29,920
and draw whatever we wanted.

418
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:32,600
Do you feel like

419
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:33,840
you're a little bit back
in your childhood now?

420
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:35,760
A little.

421
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:37,660
(Smiles)

422
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:39,680
Actually, I think flying a kite

423
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:41,680
is one of the moments
I remember most clearly.

424
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:43,800
While I was flying it,

425
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:46,240
I suddenly went
from being seven to my teens,

426
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:47,640
twelve or thirteen,

427
00:14:47,640 --> 00:14:49,400
then somehow to fifteen or sixteen.

428
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,920
With the kite string in your hand,

429
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:52,880
it feels like you're traveling
through time.

430
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:57,320
And then you're back in the present.

431
00:14:58,400 --> 00:14:58,920
Yeah.

432
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:00,580
(Smiles)

433
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,040
Can you guess what this is?

434
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:13,840
What?

435
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:15,360
It's a little bird.

436
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:16,680
A swallow.

437
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,040
It's kind of abstract.

438
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:20,320
Two swallows.

439
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,320
Yeah, two swallows.

440
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:23,860
(Compliment)
Very lifelike.

441
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:32,520
Is there anything
you want to draw on this?

442
00:15:33,920 --> 00:15:35,120
Something I just thought of.

443
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,320
How would you rate your mood today?

444
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:38,000
(Checking)

445
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,160
What's the highest score?

446
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:40,120
Ten.

447
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:41,600
Okay.

448
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:49,660
(Glances)

449
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:56,220
(Covering)

450
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:57,040
Let me see.

451
00:15:57,860 --> 00:15:58,720
(Cui Yihang)

452
00:15:58,720 --> 00:15:59,960
Ten is already the highest score.

453
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:00,900
I've already hit the top.

454
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:01,700
After spending some time here,

455
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:03,040
I've already doubled that.

456
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:04,880
Maybe I'll have to double it again.

457
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:06,160
Do you get how my math works?

458
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:08,060
(Glances)

459
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:09,800
(Avoiding eye contact)
Anything else?

460
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:14,560
Do you feel like
you're a little quieter today?

461
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,560
You mean the colors?

462
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:18,760
No.

463
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:20,120
I mean you.

464
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:21,360
Or are you usually

465
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:22,960
more or less like this?

466
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:25,000
No, I'm still a little nervous.

467
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:26,980
(A little nervous being with you)

468
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,240
A little nervous?

469
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:28,760
Yeah.

470
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:35,880
Anything else?

471
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:36,880
Let me think.

472
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:41,440
Pick a color you like most from here.

473
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:44,080
Write it on this.

474
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:44,880
Sure.

475
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:55,940
(Making eye contact)

476
00:16:58,320 --> 00:16:59,440
One, two, three.

477
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:01,320
You like pink too?

478
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:02,960
(Wu Siying & Cui Yihang: Pink)
Which pink did you just pick?

479
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:03,440
No.

480
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:04,280
I feel like

481
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:06,800
you're more like pink.

482
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:10,020
(You're more like pink)

483
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:20,600
The rain stopped.

484
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:22,320
It did. Let's go try it.

485
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:24,240
Little dog.

486
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:26,480
It can be our audience.

487
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:28,640
What do you think its name is?

488
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:30,760
(Glances)
I think its name should be...

489
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:31,400
Hippo.

490
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,440
(Changing his mind in one second)
Hippo.

491
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:33,840
You...

492
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:34,800
Hippo.

493
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:35,240
So I named him.

494
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:35,680
Shake.

495
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:37,200
Shake hand.

496
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:39,280
(Cold and aloof)
He ignores us.

497
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:39,840
Brother Hippo.

498
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:42,900
(Turns its head)

499
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:44,280
Have you eaten enough today?

500
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:46,400
But he actually isn't afraid of people.

501
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:47,760
Yeah, Brother Hippo.

502
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:51,240
Then let's let Hippo
watch us fly the kite.

503
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:53,800
I'll give it a try.

504
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:08,580
(Lands)

505
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:16,360
But I think you did get it up just now.

506
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:17,200
It's a little difficult.

507
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,640
It's already pretty high.

508
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,560
From where I'm standing,
it's really high.

509
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:26,040
The wind's coming from this side.

510
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:29,280
So I should do it like this. Yeah.

511
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:32,040
Do you want to give it a try?

512
00:18:32,060 --> 00:18:33,300
(Inviting)

513
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:34,120
Sure.

514
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:34,920
It's just a little tiring.

515
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:37,880
When you let out the string,
watch this part.

516
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:39,640
(Moves closer)

517
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:40,680
Just hold it down like this.

518
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:44,500
(Takes it)

519
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:46,320
And if you want to stop it,

520
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:47,920
just flick it once.

521
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:49,720
I'll hold this for you.

522
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,440
One, two, three.

523
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:00,800
It's up!

524
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:01,920
It really is!

525
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:18,540
(Mutual Date Liang Xiaoyu & Chen Hewen)

526
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:20,320
I felt like my first day here

527
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:22,520
was really a dream.

528
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:24,560
It really felt like a dream.

529
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:26,200
Were you nervous?

530
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:31,360
Not really.

531
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,040
Because I felt like

532
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:34,720
everyone would be nice,

533
00:19:34,720 --> 00:19:36,320
so I still felt

534
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:37,440
very safe.

535
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:39,600
So how do you say that
in a Northeastern accent?

536
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:40,680
Generous.

537
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:42,660
(Laughs)

538
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:46,800
I have a question
I've been curious about.

539
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:49,120
Go ahead.

540
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:50,280
You said you're often

541
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:52,760
traveling between two places.

542
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:56,160
Which one makes you

543
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:58,320
really feel at home?

544
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:00,080
It has to be Beijing.

545
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,000
I grew up in Beijing.

546
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:04,200
Hangzhou

547
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:05,240
might feel different to me

548
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,360
from what Beijing

549
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:07,120
feels like.

550
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:09,160
I do feel like Beijing

551
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:11,000
gives me that sense of home.

552
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:14,400
When you've been there too long,
you want to leave,

553
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:16,520
but once you're out,
you want to go back.

554
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:17,360
Exactly.

555
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:18,680
So I think this lifestyle
works pretty well for me.

556
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,360
I'll be away for a month,

557
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:21,480
or just away for a while,

558
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:22,620
then come back for a few days,

559
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:23,720
- then head out again.
- Exactly.

560
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:27,240
Always looking forward
to the next place.

561
00:20:27,520 --> 00:20:28,320
Yeah.

562
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:31,080
Do you

563
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:32,480
ever get homesick?

564
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:33,520
A little now.

565
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:36,720
Maybe it's because
of the past six months.

566
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:39,640
I'm usually flying back and forth,

567
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:41,800
and the more I travel,
the more I feel like

568
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:43,520
there's one constant center

569
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:45,360
in your universe.

570
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:46,600
Over the past year,

571
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:47,960
I've been going home more often.

572
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:50,240
Yeah, going home more often.

573
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:53,120
I often want to go home

574
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:54,280
to see my grandparents,

575
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:57,280
just to spend more time with them.

576
00:20:57,920 --> 00:20:59,240
I feel like

577
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:01,440
the older I get, the more I realize

578
00:21:01,440 --> 00:21:04,360
we all need something in life

579
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:05,240
to believe in,

580
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:08,480
or something that keeps us grounded.

581
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:08,800
Yeah.

582
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:10,000
I feel the same way.

583
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:11,360
We really do need that.

584
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:14,840
Let's go.

585
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:15,600
Okay.

586
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:20,080
Do you think there are things

587
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:21,400
your parents say,

588
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:22,800
or certain moments,

589
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:23,640
that make you feel

590
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:26,040
like you've earned their approval?

591
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:29,640
Actually, neither of my parents

592
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:30,640
is very good at expressing themselves.

593
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:33,800
So I just try not
to make them worry about me.

594
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:35,560
I think
I'm in a pretty good place right now.

595
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:38,160
I have my own career to focus on,

596
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:39,400
and I have my own ideas.

597
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:41,760
They're all positive and optimistic.

598
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:42,920
From a parent's perspective,

599
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:44,480
they probably don't need you
to achieve anything huge.

600
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:46,560
As long as you're doing well,

601
00:21:46,560 --> 00:21:47,720
staying in a good place mentally,

602
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:49,480
and keeping yourself busy
and fulfilled every day,

603
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:51,600
they'll feel like you're doing great.

604
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:56,920
Do you remember my question?

605
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:57,880
Wait.

606
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:58,500
(Turning)

607
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:02,080
Let's drive first.

608
00:22:02,480 --> 00:22:04,400
That's what happens
when I start talking.

609
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:05,720
I can go off on all kinds of tangents.

610
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:06,200
You know?

611
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:06,960
I know. It's okay.

612
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:08,560
I'll bring you back.

613
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:09,040
It's okay.

614
00:22:09,040 --> 00:22:10,640
I'll bring you back.

615
00:22:14,260 --> 00:22:14,840
That's just how I am.

616
00:22:14,840 --> 00:22:15,560
I'm telling you,

617
00:22:15,560 --> 00:22:16,560
once I get talking, I just wander off.

618
00:22:16,560 --> 00:22:17,520
My mind just goes somewhere else.

619
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:18,280
No problem.

620
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:19,520
I'll pull you back.

621
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:30,560
You should sing a song I know.

622
00:22:31,080 --> 00:22:32,240
One that you know?

623
00:22:32,240 --> 00:22:33,000
Just sing whatever you want.

624
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:33,840
I'll know it.

625
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:35,240
Let me think.

626
00:22:36,280 --> 00:22:39,880
♪Sparrows outside the window♪

627
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:43,360
♪Chatter away on the telephone wires♪

628
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:46,600
♪You say♪

629
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:49,960
♪This feels just like summer♪

630
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:52,720
♪The pencil in my hand♪

631
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:56,240
♪Moves back and forth♪

632
00:22:56,240 --> 00:23:02,000
♪Across the page♪

633
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:02,760
Great.

634
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:03,480
That's awesome.

635
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:05,600
You have a beautiful voice.

636
00:23:05,620 --> 00:23:07,660
(Don't go anywhere. The next episode
is even more romantic)
